				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 23,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"description": "Water Drops - view straight down onto a water surface. A real wave simulation (wave equation via feedback, two steps per frame, half resolution, 32-bit float): every drop falls away from the viewer (shrinks), hits the surface and sends out a train of rings that interfere with each other and reflect at the screen edges. No drop = the water calms down and stands still. Drop: every rising edge over 0.5 releases one drop (map a button, MIDI note, FFT kick or BPM ramp). Drop X \/ Y: impact point, 0 = centre, -1 \/ 1 = screen edge. Spread: random scatter around X \/ Y per drop (0 = always the same point). Drop Size: size of the drop and its crater. Drop Strength: height of the waves. Fall Frames: frames the drop falls before impact (0 = instant). Damping: how long the waves last (0.999 = very long). Relief: how steep the waves look. Shine: sun glints on the crests. Light Angle: direction of the light. Wave Color: sky reflection and light on the waves. Backdrop On\/Off: On = the water surface in Backdrop Color (deep water, shaded by the waves); Off = only the waves are drawn, flat water is transparent. Note: wave speed follows the frame rate. Shaders WaterSim.fs and WaterRender.fs must stay next to the patch.",
			"displayName": "Water Drops",
			"identifier": "1f37ad36-c772-4709-ba6c-92ecd71b03f4",
			"licenseName": "",
			"mail": "",
